{"type":"standard","title":"Seth Magaziner","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Seth Magaziner</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q16222460","titles":{"canonical":"Seth_Magaziner","normalized":"Seth Magaziner","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Seth Magaziner</span></span>"},"pageid":41774861,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Seth_Magaziner_%281%29.jpg/330px-Seth_Magaziner_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":413},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/72/Seth_Magaziner_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":1638,"height":2048},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1351722086","tid":"1d25d024-43fd-11f1-95fb-ca063ec8ff3e","timestamp":"2026-04-29T18:56:22Z","description":"American politician (born 1983)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seth_Magaziner","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seth_Magaziner?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seth_Magaziner?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Seth_Magaziner"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seth_Magaziner","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Seth_Magaziner","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seth_Magaziner?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Seth_Magaziner"}},"extract":"Seth Michael Magaziner is an American investment professional and politician serving as the U.S. representative for Rhode Island's 2nd congressional district since 2023. A member of the Democratic Party, he previously served as the 31st general treasurer of Rhode Island from 2015 until 2023. Magaziner won the November 2022 election to succeed retiring representative James Langevin.","extract_html":"<p><b>Seth Michael Magaziner</b> is an American investment professional and politician serving as the U.S. representative for Rhode Island's 2nd congressional district since 2023. A member of the Democratic Party, he previously served as the 31st general treasurer of Rhode Island from 2015 until 2023. Magaziner won the November 2022 election to succeed retiring representative James Langevin.</p>"}